---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase, site } from '../../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Yaya Etiabi's research background, academic experience, teaching, mentoring and scientific activities."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Background &amp; academic activities</div>
      <h1>About me</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I am a researcher working at the intersection of machine learning and wireless communications.
        I hold a PhD in Computer Science and an engineering degree in Electrical Engineering,
        with a specialization in embedded systems and telecommunications.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container page-content">
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Academic and research background</h2>
        <p>
          My research began with distributed localization methods for Internet of Things (IoT)
          networks. During my PhD at Mohammed VI Polytechnic University (UM6P), completed in
          2025, I focused on machine learning for collaborative and privacy-preserving wireless
          localization. This work included federated learning, meta-learning and federated
          distillation methods for adapting localization models to different environments and
          reducing the communication required for collaborative training. I also pursued
          related research during an internship at ISEP in Paris.
        </p>
        <p>
          My postdoctoral research at Université du Québec à Montréal (UQAM) in 2025–2026
          broadened this work toward AI-native wireless systems and Edge Intelligence.
          I am particularly interested in the joint design of sensing, communication and
          computation for learning and inference, as well as radio-based sensing and
          localization. These directions build on my earlier research while addressing
          different questions at the intersection of AI and wireless systems.
        </p>

        <h2>Research approach</h2>
        <p>
          I work across the research process, from defining a problem and developing a
          method to implementing experiments and assessing the results. My work draws
          on wireless-system simulations and experimental datasets, with evaluations
          grounded in quantitative comparisons, including accuracy, adaptation,
          communication overhead and computational cost where relevant.
          The <a href={withBase('/research/')}>Research</a>,
          <a href={withBase('/projects/')}>Projects</a> and
          <a href={withBase('/publications/')}>Publications</a> pages provide the
          technical details and research outputs.
        </p>

        <h2>Teaching and academic contribution</h2>
        <p>
          Teaching, mentoring and student research supervision are part of my academic
          experience. I have contributed to programming and machine learning education
          and guided student research from the development of research questions through
          implementation, evaluation and presentation of results.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also contribute to academic peer review and conference technical program
          activities. More about this work is available on the
          <a href={withBase('/teaching-outreach/')}>Teaching &amp; Outreach page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Scientific communication and community involvement</h2>
        <p>
          I have presented research at international conferences and academic events,
          including scientific communication competitions. I was a finalist in the
          IEEE ComSoc Three Minute Thesis competition at IEEE ICC 2023 and received
          presentation awards at UM6P Doctoral Days and a MOMI event at Inria.
          The <a href={withBase('/talks/')}>Talks &amp; Presentations page</a>
          documents these activities.
        </p>
        <p>
          My involvement in AI education also extends to community classes, webinars
          and public discussions. I have facilitated and mentored participants in
          Black in AI's Emerging Leaders in AI program and contribute to the scientific
          and thematic content of AURA Association.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="sidebar-panel" aria-label="Explore profile and related work">
        <h3>Explore my work</h3>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/research/')}>Research directions ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/projects/')}>Research projects ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/publications/')}>Publications ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/talks/')}>Talks &amp; Presentations ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/teaching-outreach/')}>Teaching &amp; Outreach ↗</a></p>
        <div class="sidebar-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h3>Academic profiles</h3>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.orcid} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ORCID ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/contact/')}>Contact ↗</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
